MID_LGV_1_M05_Kai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Kai_m01_001: It was fun to use the training grounds for the first\ntime. I liked trying out different fighting styles.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Kai_m01_002: Till now, I only ever trained with my dad, so this was\ntotally different, and kinda great.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Kai_m01: <BLN>It was fun...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Bel_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Bel_m01_001: To prevail in a fight, you need strength that\noutmatches your enemy's.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Bel_m01_002: Now, time for me to master the weapon once\nwielded by a great king.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Bel_m01: <BLN>I will master it.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Dit_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Dit_m01_001: At times, my soul thirsts uncontrollably...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Dit_m01_002: All color is leeched from the world. The merest task\nbecomes a burden.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Dit_m01_003: If this befell you, how would you slake your thirst?
MID_LGV_1_M05_Dit_m01_004: <NCA>Suggest a good meal and a nap.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Dit_m01_005: <NCB>Say that the soul must seek satisfaction.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Dit_m01_006: <ACA>Those are the means to satisfy the body... Such\nthings will not slake the thirst I speak of.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Dit_m01_007: <ACB>That is correct. My blade and I must seek it—the\nblood of the strong!
MID_LGA_1_M05_Dit_m01: <BLN>This thirst, it consumes me.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Tal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Tal_m01_001: It's more than choosing the right beans that makes a\ngood cup of coffee. Brewing is an art like any other.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Tal_m01_002: And it takes an artist with a talented hand to make\nanything truly worth the sip.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Tal_m01_003: But the sunset-colored stuff will always be my\nfavorite. Heh. Could go for a cup right now...
MID_LGA_1_M05_Tal_m01: <BLN>Ever had coffee?
MID_LGV_1_M05_Orh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Orh_m01_001: The capital has such a festive mood. I love the\nbustling market—and hearing singing now and then!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Orh_m01_002: Just strolling the city makes me so happy, though...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Orh_m01_003: I broke into dance the other day, right in the middle\nof the city.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Orh_m01_004: By the time I realized what I was doing, I was so\nembarrassed, and Diego was somewhat annoyed too.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Orh_m01: <BLN>I'm having a wonderful time!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Seo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Seo_m01_001: Even outside Saramis, there are few in Dagda who\nare my equal in allure.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Seo_m01_002: Yet when I looked upon the statue of Yu Phas in her\ntemple, I saw one who surpassed me.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Seo_m01_003: Her face had the dignity of one who governs souls,\ncouched in a gentle demeanor. Mine cannot compare.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Seo_m01: <BLN>I cannot compare to her.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Led_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Led_m01_001: I knew anyone participating in the Heroic Games\nwould be strong.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Led_m01_002: A dainty little bard like me will have to bulk up if I\nwant to win...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Led_m01_003: *sigh* If only I could win this competition by batting\nmy eyelashes and making my opponents roll over.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Led_m01: <BLN>This isn't going to be easy.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Anh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Anh_m01_001: I touched real silk for the first time when I visited\nthe market. I understand now why it's so valuable.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Anh_m01_002: The shopkeep convinced me to feel the silk.\nIt was so smooth!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Anh_m01_003: I've been told my hair is like silk, but I think that's\nfar too generous.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Anh_m01: <BLN>It was real...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Tia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Tia_m01_001: That older gentleman was being quite loud about\nhow he didn't want to see me around again.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Tia_m01_002: If he doesn't want to see me, perhaps he ought to be\nwearing a patch over BOTH his eyes.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Tia_m01: <BLN>Really, I've had enough!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Pet_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Pet_m01_001: Fights are scary. I don't like getting hurt and, if I'm\nhonest, I don't like being in the Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Pet_m01_002: But I do think it's cool to have people watching.\nAll the fancy arena gimmicks are neat too.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Pet_m01: <BLN>Maybe it's not all bad...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Hur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Hur_m01_001: Cai's really something, isn't he? Standing alongside\nqueens and foreign swordsmen...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Hur_m01_002: In the beginning, I didn't think any of this would\nwork. But they passed the exam and here we are.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Hur_m01: <BLN>Cai's really something...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Max_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Max_m01_001: Heya, how's it going? Boy, is the Infernal Clown\nfeeling greaaat!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Max_m01_002: Makes me wanna dance. You ever get like that?
MID_LGV_1_M05_Max_m01_003: Your emotions take over, and ya just wanna twirl\naround with someone and a couple of blades!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Max_m01_004: <NCA>Agree with him.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Max_m01_005: <NCB>Ask if he's serious.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Max_m01_006: <ACA>Heh heh HEH! I knew you were like me.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Max_m01_007: <ACB>Heh, 'course I am. But it's fine—different strokes.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Max_m01: <BLN>How's it going?
MID_LGV_1_M05_Gol_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Gol_m01_001: Bwahaha! I went to the marketplace and bought all\nthe smoked meat I could carry!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Gol_m01_002: They said they beefed up their stock for the games.\nNow I won't want for snacks when I'm drinkin'!
MID_LGA_1_M05_Gol_m01: <BLN>Great shopping trip!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Gat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Gat_m01_001: It's interesting that some have come from beyond\nDagda's shores to prove their skill.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Gat_m01_002: When I was young, I likewise crossed the sea on a\njourney to train. I suppose warriors are alike in that.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Gat_m01: <BLN>That's the warrior's nature.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Dan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Dan_m01_001: The arena is like a blazing forge that refines all the\ngladiators who enter.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Dan_m01_002: Inevitably, they emerge from it hardened! Though\nsome, like the Butcher, are relegated to lesser roles.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Dan_m01_003: But the Heroic Games are not merely a contest of\ngladiators. It has soldiers, royals, priests—children!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Dan_m01_004: One sees clashes between people of all kinds.\nHumanity at its most naked and true! So inspiring...
MID_LGA_1_M05_Dan_m01: <BLN>It is almost beyond words!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Fab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Fab_m01_001: If tricked, only a fool would curse the one who\ntricked them.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Fab_m01_002: Yet so many of the beasts in this place crow and\nbray—demonstrating only their foolishness. Pitiful.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Fab_m01: <BLN>Pitiful, is it not?
MID_LGV_1_M05_Esm_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Esm_m01_001: Both the kingdom of Saramis and the Vandahl\nTrading Company have incredible ships.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Esm_m01_002: Even so, I'm not sure they're good enough to take on\nCetus, the Sea Tyrant.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Esm_m01_003: Not that it matters. If we asked, it's not like they'd\nlend us one of them!
MID_LGA_1_M05_Esm_m01: <BLN>Not the fishing boats I'm used to!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Urs_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Urs_m01_001: I try to discover as much as I can about our rivals.\nMore information means better preparation.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Urs_m01_002: Of course, they may attempt to deceive you, but\nthat's to be expected.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Urs_m01_003: Anticipating competition, recognizing authenticity.\nThat's what makes a good manager.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Urs_m01: <BLN>What makes a good manager...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Sim_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Sim_m01_001: Some people are shocked that kids are fighting in the\ngames. Must be nice to be so sheltered.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Sim_m01_002: If you're good enough to get in the arena, you're a\nbetter fighter than most adults.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Sim_m01: <BLN>I mean, it's not THAT rare...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lou_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lou_m01_001: The imperial city is amazing! You can even find rare\ngoods here for a pretty reasonable price.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lou_m01_002: The food, the clothes, the theater! But the best thing\nof all is that there's so much water!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lou_m01_003: If your hands get dirty, you can just rinse them off\nright away! Isn't it great?
MID_LGA_1_M05_Lou_m01: <BLN>I love this place!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Fia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Fia_m01_001: When I was rescued, I was told that I'd collapsed by\nthe river. But...why was I there to begin with?
MID_LGV_1_M05_Fia_m01_002: Apparently I'd slipped into the water and... And...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Fia_m01_003: It's no good... I can't remember anything.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Fia_m01: <BLN>What happened to me...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Die_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Die_m01_001: What are you looking at? Think there's something\nfunny about what I'm wearing?
MID_LGV_1_M05_Die_m01_002: The details of what I'm wearing are crafted to ward\noff all sorts of dangers—from arrows to curses.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Die_m01_003: That's why I don't remove any of it. The temple\npriests always complain about it. So annoying...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Die_m01_004: <NCA>Tell Diego he shouldn't care.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Die_m01_005: <NCB>Suggest he ask a god to stop them.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Die_m01_006: <ACA>I couldn't agree more. Their opinions are worthless\nto me anyway.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Die_m01_007: <ACB>I suppose I could ask Credna, but I'd never ask him\nabout something so trivial.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Die_m01_008: Uggh. The old scar on my back is acting up...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Die_m01_009: This have anything to do with HIM too? He said\nhe was turning into the demon god...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Die_m01_010: It's as if the past is wounding me afresh... Like it's\nwarning me to remember my old days.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Die_m01_011: <NCA>Tell him to move on from the past.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Die_m01_012: <NCB>Tell him to have it healed by magic.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Die_m01_013: <ACA>You think I don't know that? I moved on a long\ntime ago.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Die_m01_014: <ACB>There's a lot more to this. Just leave me alone,\nQueen of Saramis.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Die_m01: <BLN>So annoying...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lor_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lor_m01_001: All the people battling in the Heroic Games look\ndangerous. But that figures!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lor_m01_002: There are bandits, for one. But I'd swear some\nfighters move like they're...not human.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lor_m01_003: Y-yeah...we b-better not have to fight monsters\nat some point!
MID_LGA_1_M05_Lor_m01: <BLN>That figures!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Set_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Set_m01_001: The Fire Ceremony is quite interesting, or so I've\nheard. I gather it takes place at Credna's temple.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Set_m01_002: The ritual centers on a special fire that his temple\nprovides. It's of special value to blacksmiths.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Set_m01_003: Thinking of that flame, I've found myself wanting to\nabandon my life as a traveler and work at a forge!
MID_LGA_1_M05_Set_m01: <BLN>A fascinating ritual.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Nin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Nin_m01_001: People die, and die often, whether in the arena or\non battlefields. It's sudden, and then it's over.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Nin_m01_002: Yu Phas... May you find all souls lost in battle and\nshepherd them to the gardens of peace...
MID_LGA_1_M05_Nin_m01: <BLN>The souls of the dead...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Bon_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Bon_m01_001: I have been doing focused research into the imperial\ncapital, and I notice many oddities.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Bon_m01_002: Not all of them stem from the difficulty of\nmaintaining public order, common to every city.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Bon_m01_003: Something has lurked in the shadows of the capital\nsince ancient times...or so it seems to me.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Bon_m01: <BLN>I feel a darkness here.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Tob_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Tob_m01_001: Gladiators in the arena, huh? I think I'd do pretty\ngood as a gladiator. The people would love me!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Tob_m01_002: But it wouldn't be much fun cooped up down there\nwith no way to go hunting or sailing.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Tob_m01_003: Yeah, I think I'm happy where I am as a commander\nof Saramis.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Tob_m01: <BLN>What if I were a gladiator?
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lil_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lil_m01_001: Now that I've left my family back in Saramis to go\nfight for the queen all over...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lil_m01_002: I can't help but wonder sometimes what they're up\nto now. Do they ever think of me?
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lil_m01_003: I don't wanna worry them... Maybe there's some way\nto show them I'm doing OK.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lil_m01_004: <NCA>Suggest a gift.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lil_m01_005: <NCB>Suggest a letter.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lil_m01_006: <ACA>Ooh, that's a good idea. Maybe I can get\na Saraminian messenger to deliver it.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lil_m01_007: <ACB>Are you making fun of me? You should know by now\nthat the people of Saramis don't read or write.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Lil_m01: <BLN>I wonder what they're up to now.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lys_m01_001: Whenever I hear of a new restaurant opening,\nI make a point to check out its menu and reputation.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lys_m01_002: It helps to be familiar with several good restaurants\nwhen asking someone out to dinner.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Lys_m01: <BLN>I try to stay informed.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Buc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Buc_m01_001: As expected, the Heroic Games' contestants all meet\nthe highest standard.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Buc_m01_002: No doubt, when the battle begins, their performance\nwill be exceptional...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Buc_m01_003: But I am beyond exceptional. They will have no luck\nwhen they face the Demon Bear.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Buc_m01: <BLN>I will not be bested.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Sci_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Sci_m01_001: Art of all kinds can be found in Kalla's temple.\nIt is a veritable trove of beauty!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Sci_m01_002: Which is why painters, sculptors, musicians, poets...\nartists of all kinds visit to pray for protection.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Sci_m01_003: Though of course, only a select few are actually\ngranted audience with Kalla.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Sci_m01: <BLN>Beauty upon beauty!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Moo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Moo_m01_001: There's so much to see in Dagsion, you'd never\nget bored!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Moo_m01_002: Sure, the temples, but also those aqueducts that go\nbeyond the city, that huuuge naval port...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Moo_m01_003: Even the paving stones—I can't stop wondering what\nquarry they came from!
MID_LGA_1_M05_Moo_m01: <BLN>There's just so MUCH!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Mic_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Mic_m01_001: It's obvious at a glance that a lot of highly skilled\nfighters have gathered from across Dagda.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Mic_m01_002: Some of their faces I've spied across the battlefield in\nmy mercenary days. Well, I'm pretty sure I did.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Mic_m01_003: This won't be easy. Not when your opponent already\nknows how you operate!
MID_LGA_1_M05_Mic_m01: <BLN>This looks tough...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Oly_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Oly_m01_001: I once visited a restaurant that had a limited-time\nspecial offering of all-you-can-eat yarc meat.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Oly_m01_002: After a leisurely meal where I ate to my heart's\ncontent, I paid the bill with plenty of time to spare.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Oly_m01_003: When I did, the owner said, with tears in his eyes,\n"Please don't come back." I wonder why!
MID_LGA_1_M05_Oly_m01: <BLN>I can't fathom it.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Naz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Naz_m01_001: I thought Dadao's size was rare. But there's lots of\nhuge people in the Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Naz_m01_002: I'm not worried. I won't lose to anyone who thinks\nthey can win fights just because they're big.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Naz_m01_003: But I'll tell you a secret. If I could get that big,\nI'd definitely do it!
MID_LGA_1_M05_Naz_m01: <BLN>I would if I could!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Sar_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Sar_m01_001: I didn't think much of it before, but maybe my\nclothes stand out quite a bit.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Sar_m01_002: I almost never see anyone else wearing clothes\nlike mine.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Sar_m01_003: <NCA>Admit they stand out.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Sar_m01_004: <NCB>Say they suit her.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Sar_m01_005: <ACA>I guess they do, don't they? I really like them, though.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Sar_m01_006: <ACA>I guess they do, don't they? I really like them, though.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Sar_m01_007: <ACB>Oh my! What a lovely compliment!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Sar_m01_008: <ACB>Oh my! What a lovely compliment!
MID_LGA_1_M05_Sar_m01: <BLN>Do I stand out too much?
MID_LGV_1_M05_Dai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Dai_m01_001: Argh! Just remembering it makes me angry!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Dai_m01_002: I found a beast caught in a trap that no one seemed\nto be minding, so I ate it. I wasn't stealing!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Dai_m01_003: But the hunter caught me eating his catch, and took\na shot at me! He even called me a sand boar!
MID_LGA_1_M05_Dai_m01: <BLN>It was terrible!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Hal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Hal_m01_001: Thanks to all my training as a performer, I can make\na living anywhere.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Hal_m01_002: It feels maybe like Nasshim's still helping me out.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Hal_m01: <BLN>Thank you, Nasshim...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Guj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Guj_m01_001: Some fool at the tavern actually asked me how long\nI was going to go on boasting of my epic life?
MID_LGV_1_M05_Guj_m01_002: That's like asking a fire, "Hey you, fire! How long\nya gonna burn there?"
MID_LGV_1_M05_Guj_m01_003: I mean, the answer is obvious. Until the very end\nwhen it's all said and done!
MID_LGA_1_M05_Guj_m01: <BLN>What a fool!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Yan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Yan_m01_001: I might have been a little tipsy, but maybe I shouldn't\nhave toppled a god's statue into Lake Baal.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Yan_m01_002: Fortunately, the authorities wrote it off as an act of\ndrunken folly. I was nearly put into a prison cell.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Yan_m01_003: I think I'll refrain from riling up the temple soldiers\nfor a while. Their interrogations are interminable!
MID_LGA_1_M05_Yan_m01: <BLN>I may have gone too far.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Iio_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Iio_m01_001: I'm not too familiar with the Saraminian people,\nbut that's not to say I find them off-putting.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Iio_m01_002: People have the freedom of devoting themselves\nto the god of their choosing.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Iio_m01_003: Where I draw the line is their taste in cuisine.\nTry as I might, I find a fish diet unpalatable.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Iio_m01: <BLN>The one thing I can't get over...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Pep_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Pep_m01_001: The lowest level of the city is bustling. We find the\nsight of its many children proof of a good country!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Pep_m01_002: Someone actually had the cheek to call us...what was\nthe phrasing? "A funny kid who talks weird!"
MID_LGA_1_M05_Pep_m01: <BLN>What life! What cheek!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Noc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Noc_m01_001: After coming to Dagsion from Mount Orgus, I used to\nget lost in the city a lot!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Noc_m01_002: Everything was so beautiful. I kept getting so\ndistracted that I'd lose track of where I was.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Noc_m01_003: I'm used to Dagsion now, so I could show you\naround if you ever lose your bearings.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Noc_m01: <BLN>Wandering the city...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Sop_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Sop_m01_001: I rarely get woozy when I drink, so my superiors\nask me to watch out for them when they do.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Sop_m01_002: But that's OK. When people get silly like that, I get a\nfew extra laughs in for the day.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Sop_m01_003: When else are you going to see people tipping over\nall of a sudden—or snoring into their drinks?
MID_LGA_1_M05_Sop_m01: <BLN>Funny temple work!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Cat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Cat_m01_001: I just can't cope with what's happening around here.\nIt's making me feel ill.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Cat_m01_002: I'd assumed that only the most splendid fighters\nwould gather for the Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Cat_m01_003: But, bandit clans and questionable generals? This \nhas made me queasy.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Cat_m01: <BLN>Feeling so queasy...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Ned_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Ned_m01_001: I've found it an education to be here for the Heroic\nGames, studying the motions of the fighters.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Ned_m01_002: The way they advance and wield their weapons...\nHow they focus and train...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Ned_m01_003: This has been a precious opportunity to meet great\nwarriors from all over—right here in this city.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Ned_m01: <BLN>I could watch this forever.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Zac_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Zac_m01_001: I'd maul the shops around here if I could. But I\ndunno if my axe is up to the task!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Zac_m01_002: Or, wait... I just gotta attack an axe shop and get\nme a better axe!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Zac_m01_003: Wait, but my axe ain't good enough for that. Damn,\nI'm never gonna figure this out!
MID_LGA_1_M05_Zac_m01: <BLN>Ready to rampage!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Maj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Maj_m01_001: I glanced at some lady earlier and nearly lost my\nmind, thinking it was that Maria!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Maj_m01_002: Damn hair! Her hair was a liar!
MID_LGA_1_M05_Maj_m01: <BLN>Got a damn scare!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Ven_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Ven_m01_001: Strange! Nobody has plied me with compliments\nabout how superior my chariot command was!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Ven_m01_002: Could they not grasp my masterful precision? Or the\nbrilliance of my intricate moves?
MID_LGV_1_M05_Ven_m01_003: The world has sunk into such a deplorable state. As\na proud general, I grieve for the future.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Ven_m01: <BLN>Are their eyes corked up?
MID_LGV_1_M05_Jas_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Jas_m01_001: Thanks to our time in the Heroic Games, our clan's\nname is getting to be well-known.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Jas_m01_002: We'll surely get lots of new contracts, and after\nthose, our name will travel even further.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Jas_m01_003: If that happens, we'll have the resources to pull our\nold crew back together in full. You wait and see!
MID_LGA_1_M05_Jas_m01: <BLN>You wait and see!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Ale_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Ale_m01_001: I've honed my skills as a temple knight for a long\ntime and wielded an Arc too. Still, I lost...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Ale_m01_002: I wasn't all that certain if fighting to repay my uncle's\nfavor was the right thing to do.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Ale_m01_003: I'd better stop stepping into battlefields if I'm feeling\nthis way. It's a disservice to Bucephalus.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Ale_m01: <BLN>I've felt uncertain.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Cen_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Cen_m01_001: My tasks are piling up. I have to direct inspections at\nthe gates, plan for night-patrol reinforcements...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Cen_m01_002: All these are sacred rituals that must go\nuninterrupted.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Cen_m01_003: I am Aurora's chief celestial general, so I must\nfocus on all temple concerns promptly.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Cen_m01: <BLN>It's my burden!
MID_LGV_1_M05_Kir_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Kir_m01_001: {SetColor=Gray}That fraud... Thinks he's so slick... Just a common\nmoney-grubber, that Talimun...{SetColor=Default}
MID_LGV_1_M05_Kir_m01_002: {SetColor=Gray}Tossing me overboard... Right into the drink...\nThe horror of it all, the horror...{SetColor=Default}
MID_LGV_1_M05_Kir_m01_003: {SetColor=Gray}I'm wrecked... Haunted... Ghosts around every\nc-corner... Curse his name forever...{SetColor=Default}
MID_LGA_1_M05_Kir_m01: <BLN>If it's the last thing I do...
MID_LGV_1_M05_Gab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Gab_m01_001: The stage for the next match is even wilder than\nusual. Gonna be a lotta work, getting the materials.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Gab_m01_002: I have to call in a lot of favors. Being able to provide\neverything's a point of pride for me.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Gab_m01_003: Yeesh. That Dante. She's always asking for the moon\nand stars.
MID_LGA_1_M05_Gab_m01: <BLN>It's wild.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lin_m01_001: Do you know the color of darkness?
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lin_m01_002: It isn't just black. True darkness is a whole range\nof murky shades intertwined.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lin_m01_003: I've gotten to know each of the hundred kinds of\ndarkness intimately.
MID_LGV_1_M05_Lin_m01_004: In this cell, there's nothing else to think about...
MID_LGA_1_M05_Lin_m01: <BLN>Do you know it like I do?
MID_LGV_1_M05_Miw_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_Miw_m01_001: Do you know of the artist Zenzele?
MID_LGV_1_M05_Miw_m01_002: If you don't, well, that's fine...
MID_LGA_1_M05_Miw_m01: <BLN>Do you know?
MID_LGV_1_M05_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B01_m01_001: Our merchant caravan has grown. It might be time\nthat we purchased some more jamels.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B01_m01_002: Their pace is slower than a horse's, but they have\nthe advantage of being able to cross deserts.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B01_m01: <BLN>We do need more jamels...
MID_LGV_1_M05_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B02_m01_001: Aww... The clan I bet a bundle on went and lost.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B02_m01_002: They'd made a real name for themselves in the\ngames, but I guess there's always someone better.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B02_m01: <BLN>I thought they could go all the way.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B03_m01_001: Another year where I received the Flame of Credna's\nHearth without a hitch.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B03_m01_002: It's burning nicely in my workshop. I find it\ninspiring to look upon.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B03_m01: <BLN>I'm glad I got it again.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B04_m01_001: I've been getting by as a mercenary up to now, but\nit's nice to finally get some cheers in the arena.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B04_m01_002: I can see what retired gladiators mean now when\nthey say they miss the place.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B04_m01: <BLN>Feels pretty good.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B05_m01_001: I'm gonna sew leaves onto my clothes so I can be\njust like Kalla!
MID_LGV_1_M05_B05_m01_002: I wanna grow up soon so I can be as pretty as her.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B05_m01: <BLN>I'm looking for leaves!
MID_LGV_1_M05_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B06_m01_001: I usually manage a backwater shrine, but I got called\nhere because they need more staff.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B06_m01_002: I never really connected with the folks out there, so it\nfeels good to be back in the thick of things.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B06_m01: <BLN>Ah, the clamor of the city!
MID_LGV_1_M05_B07_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B07_m01_001: I'd hesitate to say this to Lord Solel's face, but I think\nwe ought to demolish Yu Phas's temple.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B07_m01_002: Yes, she was Lord Solel's wife, but the Divine\nEmperor personally put her to death.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B07_m01_003: What does it say of the gods' commitment to the law\nto leave intact a temple to a heretical deity?
MID_LGA_1_M05_B07_m01: <BLN>Should I bring it up?
MID_LGV_1_M05_B08_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B08_m01_001: Urgh, I was assigned to watch out from the\nlookout platform.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B08_m01_002: I'm not great with heights... It's why I abandoned the\nidea of being a wing soldier.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B08_m01: <BLN>It's gonna be rough.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B09_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B09_m01_001: Even a grand religious celebration in the capital can't\nhide the strange things happening across Dagda.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B09_m01_002: In the last decade, the kings of both Saramis and\nArago were assassinated. Brezarant still has no ruler.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B09_m01_003: I hope all of this isn't a sign of some terrible disaster\nin the offing...
MID_LGA_1_M05_B09_m01: <BLN>It's disturbing when you add it up.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B10_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B10_m01_001: Day after day, all I see is folks shuffling around\nlooking like easy marks.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B10_m01_002: Make yourself a target and you can't go crying to\nanyone when I make you a victim.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B10_m01: <BLN>Can you really blame me?
MID_LGV_1_M05_B11_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B11_m01_001: Every time I come to this district, all I see are public\ndisorder and unsavory characters. It beggars belief. 
MID_LGV_1_M05_B11_m01_002: Is there no faith in their souls? Clearly, they need a\nsermon on the honor in worshipping the divine.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B11_m01: <BLN>Every time, it's the same thing...
MID_LGV_1_M05_B12_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B12_m01_001: Credna's statue doesn't really inspire me to pray\nto him. But Mars is so cool.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B12_m01_002: He's famous as the god of war, and super strong and\npowerful. I wonder if he's single...
MID_LGA_1_M05_B12_m01: <BLN>Mars is the one for me...
MID_LGV_1_M05_B13_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B13_m01_001: It's a tough job to maintain the water supply. But it's\nsomething I can be proud of.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B13_m01_002: If we didn't stick it out every day getting wet, life in\nthe capital wouldn't be the same.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B13_m01: <BLN>It's not glamorous work, but...
MID_LGV_1_M05_B14_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B14_m01_001: The garum that we usually use is thick and viscous,\nbut the stuff the temples get is different.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B14_m01_002: Said to be properly strained, golden yellow, and\nsmooth as silk. Gah! I want to try it!
MID_LGA_1_M05_B14_m01: <BLN>I've never seen it, but...
MID_LGV_1_M05_B15_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B15_m01_001: When I was a child, I got told off for trying to climb\nthe statue of the goddess.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B15_m01_002: Thinking back, I can see how it was disrespectful.\nI hope I don't get smote.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B15_m01: <BLN>I was just a foolish kid...
MID_LGV_1_M05_B16_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B16_m01_001: Some temple staff let me borrow a horse, since I had\nmore to haul than I expected.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B16_m01_002: He's a good boy, and obedient too! I've only had him\na few days, but I'm already pretty attached.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B16_m01_003: I wonder if they'd sell him to me. Even if it costs me\neverything I have, he's worth it!
MID_LGA_1_M05_B16_m01: <BLN>What a great horse!
MID_LGV_1_M05_B17_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B17_m01_001: I met a beautiful woman when I wandered into\na tavern in lowtown...
MID_LGV_1_M05_B17_m01_002: I got so swept up in her thrilling stories of her travels\nthat I lost track of the time.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B17_m01: <BLN>Perhaps we'll meet again...
MID_LGV_1_M05_B18_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B18_m01_001: My family were imperial financiers, but that was\nlong ago. I'd like to get a political foothold again...
MID_LGV_1_M05_B18_m01_002: It's too late for my generation, but there might be\nhope for my children if I educate them strictly.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B18_m01: <BLN>It's up to my children now.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B19_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B19_m01_001: The delicacies that Mandalan Trading stocks are\nwonderful. They satisfy even my palate.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B19_m01_002: Where in the world do they get them? I want to ask,\nbut I fear it would be tactless of me.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B19_m01_003: It could well be some illicit route...not that that would\nmake me stop buying them. Hahaha!
MID_LGA_1_M05_B19_m01: <BLN>Better to look the other way.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B20_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B20_m01_001: It's not clear exactly when people started vanishing\nfrom Aurora's temple.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B20_m01_002: But the rumor is that Aurora herself may be behind\nit all.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B20_m01_003: That seems to be the agreed-upon reason why she's\nshut up in the temple and never makes appearances.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B20_m01: <BLN>It's one juicy rumor.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B21_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B21_m01_001: The Talto River and Sobek River flow north and\nsouth from Lake Baal, respectively.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B21_m01_002: Both of those great rivers are used as waterways,\nletting ships come and go safely.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B21_m01_003: But it's comparatively rare for the sluice gate that\nexits to the north to be opened.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B21_m01: <BLN>Lake Baal feeds two rivers.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B22_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B22_m01_001: The land of Dagda is controlled by the Dagdan\npantheon, headed by the Divine Emperor.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B22_m01_002: But are things the same in Fódlan? Do they have\ntheir own Fódlan pantheon?
MID_LGA_1_M05_B22_m01: <BLN>I'm not so sure...
MID_LGV_1_M05_B23_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B23_m01_001: Fortune-telling's really taken off in this city lately.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B23_m01_002: What is it people hope to gain from such foolishness?
MID_LGA_1_M05_B23_m01: <BLN>What's the value in it?
MID_LGV_1_M05_B24_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B24_m01_001: Why is Fortuna's temple the only one you can't reach\nfrom Temple Row?
MID_LGV_1_M05_B24_m01_002: I've heard some claim that it's located farther back,\nbehind Dagda's temple.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B24_m01_003: Almost like she's observing the Divine Emperor\nfrom the shadows...
MID_LGV_1_M05_B24_m01_004: But I must be overthinking this. Right?
MID_LGA_1_M05_B24_m01: <BLN>I have my suspicions...
MID_LGV_1_M05_B25_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B25_m01_001: I hear that a beautiful woman sometimes plays the\nvihuela in this city's taverns.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B25_m01_002: It must be quite a show. I'd love to catch her act in\nperson, just once.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B25_m01: <BLN>Where will she play next?
MID_LGV_1_M05_B26_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B26_m01_001: There are many splendid temples to be found here.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B26_m01_002: But travel abroad, and you'll encounter completely\ndifferent faiths.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B26_m01_003: Despite my appearance, I'm a devout believer in\nSeiros. But the Dagdan faith is also of great interest.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B26_m01: <BLN>Different lands, different faiths.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B27_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B27_m01_001: Have you ever walked through a desert? Visibility is\nterrible, thanks to the sandstorms.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B27_m01_002: Be very careful when traveling out there. You can\nlose your way before you know it.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B27_m01_003: Make sure you take all the necessary precautions.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B27_m01: <BLN>Never underestimate the desert.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B28_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B28_m01_001: If you get certified in a new class, expect your\nstrength to increase by leaps and bounds.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B28_m01_002: For example, imagine an ally is especially good at\nmagic. They become a diviner and polish their skills.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B28_m01_003: Just as a priest is promoted to lead priest, so too can\none climb the ranks of other professions.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B28_m01_004: The skills required for certification vary. Some might\neven require high proficiency in multiple skills.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B28_m01_005: It's wise to decide on a class you'd like to reach, and\nthen think about what skills you'll need to get there.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B28_m01: <BLN>Taken any certification exams?
MID_LGV_1_M05_B29_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B29_m01_001: Have you ever seen a giant? They're monsters that\nare found more commonly out west.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B29_m01_002: They're a real threat, capable of smashing up a small\nsettlement in only a few minutes.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B29_m01_003: A good few villages have been wiped off the map—\nthe houses razed and their inhabitants eaten.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B29_m01: <BLN>Have you ever seen a giant?
MID_LGV_1_M05_B30_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B30_m01_001: There are apparently treasures out there that grant\ntheir wielders dominion over the world.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B30_m01_002: They say the Pirate King Drake used such things to\nreign over the Danann Sea long ago.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B30_m01: <BLN>Such wondrous artifacts...
MID_LGV_1_M05_B31_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B31_m01_001: In the Dagdan Empire, one of the most exalted titles\nis "Flame Lord of Dagda."
MID_LGV_1_M05_B31_m01_002: It's given to warriors who accomplish especially\nremarkable feats.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B31_m01_003: Only the Divine Emperor or the Divine Sovereign\ncan award it. It comes with a unique epithet as well.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B31_m01: <BLN>Do you know about Flame Lords?
MID_LGV_1_M05_B32_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B32_m01_001: Except for Dagda's temple, all the temples in Dagsion\nare branch temples.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B32_m01_002: Each region of Dagda is home to its resident god's\nmain temple.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B32_m01_003: And beyond those, there are also simple shrines\nmaintained in each region.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B32_m01_004: That way, citizens who live far from the larger\ntemples can still demonstrate proper worship.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B32_m01: <BLN>These aren't the only temples.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B33_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B33_m01_001: The hero Arago founded the kingdom of the same\nname. It has the longest history of the vassal states.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B33_m01_002: Arago was a demigod, born from the Divine Emperor\nand a human, and his adventures are legendary.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B33_m01_003: Among the Aragonian kings after him, King Hanno\nis particularly famous for his match before the gods.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B33_m01_004: Let's...not talk about what became of him after that.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B33_m01: <BLN>Arago has a long history.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B34_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B34_m01_001: Fortuna is an enigma. For one thing, it is exceedingly\nrare for her to make public appearances.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B34_m01_002: She seems to generally be something of an outlier\namong the Dagdan pantheon.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B34_m01_003: But I can't put my finger on why.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B34_m01: <BLN>Fortuna is an enigma...
MID_LGV_1_M05_B35_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B35_m01_001: The temples hold numerous Arcs. Many of them\nwere crafted by Credna, the god of blacksmithing.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B35_m01_002: Credna also designed Dagsion and its aqueducts,\nand created the Gates of the Gods.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B35_m01_003: He has given us so many wondrous things that are\nbeyond the human mind.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B35_m01: <BLN>There are many Arcs...
MID_LGV_1_M05_B36_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B36_m01_001: I'm tired of seeing you around. Take a hike.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B36_m01: <BLN>Get outta my face.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B37_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M05_B37_m01_001: The master of this temple, Lord Solel, carries out his\nduties as Divine Sovereign from Dagda's temple.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B37_m01_002: For that reason, this temple is closed while he is out\non official business.
MID_LGV_1_M05_B37_m01_003: I suspect this will be the policy until the Divine\nEmperor awakens from his slumber.
MID_LGA_1_M05_B37_m01: <BLN>This temple is closed.